    <p>I think you're doing two things in the 2 lines above and the list
      below:</p>
    <p>&nbsp;1. splitting up the testargs into one per line</p>
    <p>&nbsp;2. adding an exclude list of tests that are know to fail.</p>
    <p>Is that true? <br>
      If so can you use two seperate variables/lists to reflect the
      different intended purpose of each list?<br>
      This should also help in maintaining each list and hopefully the
      tests that are exluded will all have a:</p>
    <p>&nbsp;&nbsp; tests/foo/bar.rs <br>
    </p>
    <p>format rather than somewhat worrying prefixes like:<br>
      &nbsp;&nbsp; compiler/rustc</p>
    <p>and <br>
    </p>
    <p>&nbsp;&nbsp; library/panic_abort</p>
